    <!-- translatable="false": the brand is what a user looks for on a home
         screen and in a list of installed apps. It is the same word in every
         language, and lint should stop asking. -->
    <string name="app_name" translatable="false">RoadAssist</string>

    <!--
      The SOS ladder's four outcomes — what a person reads at the worst moment
      they will ever use this app.

      These are extracted, and translated, ahead of the rest of the UI on
      purpose: the same reasoning as the server's message catalogue, which
      localised SMS and OTP before anything on a screen. Someone who cannot read
      the result of pressing SOS cannot tell whether help is coming.

      The remaining UI strings are still hardcoded English in MainActivity.kt.
      That is stated in app/docs/TESTING.md rather than left to be discovered.
    -->
    <string name="sos_sms_sent">Also texted RoadAssist at %1$s. A text is not confirmed help, so 112 and the saved copy still stand.</string>
    <string name="sos_sms_unconfirmed">Also tried to text RoadAssist at %1$s; delivery is not confirmed.</string>
    <string name="sos_dialer">Opening 112. It connects through any tower. Your SOS is also saved on this phone and goes to RoadAssist once you are online and signed in, while the app is running.</string>
    <string name="sos_queued">112 could not be opened on this phone: call 112 from any phone you can. Your SOS is saved here and goes to RoadAssist once you are online and signed in, while the app is running.</string>

